EIDAToolkit Android Libraries
=============================

EIDAToolkit.aar  - Main toolkit AAR (arm64-v8a + armeabi-v7a)
toolkit_face/    - Face verification source (Kotlin/Java)

Runtime dependency: Gson (handled transitively for project-style deps)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
EIDAToolkit.aar references com.google.gson.* in its digital-signature
data models (PadesSigningContext, VerificationContext,
PDFSigningParameters, SigningContext, etc.). The AAR does NOT bundle
Gson.

If you consume the toolkit via the AAR-shim Gradle module (the
recommended path used by samples/ToolkitSample):

    implementation project(':EIDAToolkit')

then Gson is pulled in transitively from EIDAToolkit/build.gradle's
"default" configuration — no explicit declaration needed.

If you consume the raw AAR file directly:

    implementation files('libs/EIDAToolkit.aar')

file-based deps bypass Gradle's transitive resolution, and you must
declare Gson manually in your app/build.gradle:

    implementation 'com.google.code.gson:gson:2.10.1'

Without Gson available on the classpath either way, Android Gradle
Plugin fails the build with:
    Failed to transform EIDAToolkit.aar to match attributes
    {artifactType=android-dex, ...}
    Execution failed for DexingNoClasspathTransform

This dependency is new in 3.1.x; releases earlier than 3.1.0 did
not require Gson.
